{"agent":"nvstate-lane","data":{"by":"nvstate-lane","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"The test claims to verify that `running` and `interrupted` are distinct, but after monkeypatching the clock so both claims are expired it asserts `running == interrupted`. With tasks `A` and `B` claimed and then their leases expired, those items are no longer live-running; they are interrupted. If the implementation follows this test, `ddflow next --state running --json` will return dead/expired claims as the running set, so a lane asking for “running” work will receive items that are actually in the interrupted set and may avoid requeuing or handling them. The expired-lease case should assert that `interrupted` contains `A` and `B` while `running` does not include them (or otherwise excludes interrupted items), not that the two sets are equal.","digest":"86a58430ad597fcd","location":"tests/test_next.py:test_state_running_is_distinct_from_interrupted","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_next.py:test_state_running_is_distinct_from_interrupted"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"2/4 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_sha":"ee3e82d371b303f5cfd0df5dc9d7e149dbed63952e3246f622bb00d891e7e4f6","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"max_chunk_chars":5000,"output_digest":"b3bd38887f310959","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/NV-next-state-filter.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T133915Z-5cdb08d5.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1,4],"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"f17e5ecbc5fc+clean","wanted":[1,2,3,4]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 2 chunk(s) were reviewed (1, 4); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"e474f1d6e8f3a952bd6b97175","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":193647,"schema":1,"subject":"NV-next-state-filter","ts":"2026-11-13T13:41:00.2035